        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.51,
          "en": "I set up here in my component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.51,
          "end": 60.753,
          "en": "So below all my servers I have filteredStatus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.89,
          "end": 65.07,
          "en": "which is an empty string at the beginning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 67.59,
          "en": "filteredStatus like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 68.88,
          "en": "So if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.88,
          "end": 71.78999999999999,
          "en": "we should see this new input field here at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.78999999999999,
          "end": 74.19,
          "en": "Let's maybe add a horizontal line below it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.19,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "just for styling reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 78.87,
          "en": "And with that, we can enter something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.87,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "but of course this does not do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 82.44,
          "en": "Now I want to build a pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.44,
          "end": 85.86,
          "en": "which I can apply to this list, somehow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.86,
          "end": 89.64,
          "en": "which allows me to then only view the servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.64,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "which do indeed fulfill the requirements here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "So to do this, I will add a new pipe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 100.11,
          "en": "And for this I will now use the CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.11,
          "end": 105.11,
          "en": "So ng generate pipe would be shortcut here or just g p.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.82,
          "end": 108.96000000000001,
          "en": "And then the name of your pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 111.003,
          "en": "and I will name it filter, filter pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.913,
          "end": 114.69,
          "en": "So by typing filter this gives me all the testing file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.69,
          "end": 118.064,
          "en": "which I don't need but then the filter pipe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.064,
          "end": 120.84,
          "en": "And there you can see it also pre-populates the name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "in my @Pipe decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 124.71,
          "en": "And it gives me this interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.71,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "and, well, it gives me this transform method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 129.66,
          "en": "in its most basic form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.66,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "So in here, I want to allow the user to filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 134.793,
          "en": "and I will indeed get an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.75,
          "end": 137.85,
          "en": "The first argument of this list of arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "and this will be what the user entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "So the filterString, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 145.07999999999998,
          "en": "and this will be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.07999999999998,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "Well, and then here I want to implement some logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "which allows me to only return the elements of the array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 153.03,
          "en": "which fulfill this argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 156.45499999999998,
          "en": "or which fulfill this filterString here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.45499999999998,
          "end": 158.85,
          "en": "where the status of the server matches this filter string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.85,
          "end": 160.05,
          "en": "to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "For this, I will first of all check if value.length",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 166.98,
          "en": "and value will here be the array of service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.98,
          "end": 168.78,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.78,
          "end": 170.25,
          "en": "this is the first important takeaway.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.25,
          "end": 171.71,
          "en": "It can also be an array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.71,
          "end": 174.84,
          "en": "it can be any data you output in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 174.84,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "So here I want to check if the value length is zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 180.09,
          "en": "so if it's empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.09,
          "end": 181.92,
          "en": "In which case I will just return value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.92,
          "end": 185.25,
          "en": "so I will basically just quit, there is nothing to display.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.25,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "And now after checking this, the interesting part happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 190.89,
          "en": "Here, I simply want to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190.89,
          "end": 195.69,
          "en": "or I want to loop through all my items in my value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.69,
          "end": 199.143,
          "en": "and value here will be an array, keep this in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 205.07,
          "en": "And then I want to check if my status of each server matches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "the filterString up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 211.98,
          "en": "So for this, I can simply check if item.status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.98,
          "end": 214.23,
          "en": "and of course you could write this more generic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 216.6,
          "en": "and pass the to be filtered property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.6,
          "end": 221.6,
          "en": "as a second argument like propName, which is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 223.41,
          "en": "And then you could simply say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 226.773,
          "en": "item propName in square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.827,
          "end": 232.41,
          "en": "So if this equals my filterString,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 234.12,
          "en": "only if this is equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.12,
          "end": 237.42000000000002,
          "en": "only in this case I want to return it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.42000000000002,
          "end": 240.36,
          "en": "So I should add a new result array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.36,
          "end": 243.36,
          "en": "this is an array I will use temporarily here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.36,
          "end": 246.633,
          "en": "and I will push new items on this result array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.633,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "So I will push any items on this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 252.21,
          "en": "which fulfill my criteria here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.21,
          "end": 254.01,
          "en": "which are or which have a status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.01,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "or a prop name in general equal to my filterString.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 260.25,
          "en": "So here I will then push item on this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 260.25,
          "end": 262.2,
          "en": "and return this result array in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.2,
          "end": 266.43,
          "en": "And therefore this result array will only hold the items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.43,
          "end": 269.82,
          "en": "where the propName I passed as a second argument here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.82,
          "end": 271.68,
          "en": "or as a third argument actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 271.68,
          "end": 274.71,
          "en": "where this propName or this value of the propName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.71,
          "end": 277.32,
          "en": "is actually equal to my filteredString.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 277.32,
          "end": 279.15,
          "en": "Now with this, the pipe is finished.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279.15,
          "end": 282.42,
          "en": "You have to make sure that it has been added to AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 282.42,
          "end": 284.37,
          "en": "I did this automatically here for me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.37,
          "end": 285.87,
          "en": "If you created it manually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 285.87,
          "end": 288.72,
          "en": "make sure that you add FilterPipe to declarations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 291.03,
          "en": "and add your import at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 291.03,
          "end": 292.86,
          "en": "And then in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 292.86,
          "end": 296.28,
          "en": "we apply it here in the ng for loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 296.28,
          "end": 297.99,
          "en": "And this might sound strange because:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 301.17,
          "en": "before, we only used it in string interpolation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 301.17,
          "end": 304.11,
          "en": "but keep in mind that I said at the beginning of this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 304.11,
          "end": 306.69,
          "en": "that pipes transform your output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 306.69,
          "end": 309.93,
          "en": "and the ng for loop is simply part of your output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 309.93,
          "end": 314.19,
          "en": "Therefore, of course you can add a pipe here to my servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 314.19,
          "end": 317.73,
          "en": "And then I simply say filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 317.73,
          "end": 320.28,
          "en": "of course we need to pass two parameters here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 320.28,
          "end": 324.54,
          "en": "The first parameter is the filteredStatus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 324.54,
          "end": 327.93,
          "en": "this property which holds my string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 327.93,
          "end": 329.43,
          "en": "for which I want to filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 329.43,
          "end": 331.71,
          "en": "And the second argument is my propName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 331.71,
          "end": 335.37,
          "en": "so this will be a string, and this string should be status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 335.37,
          "end": 338.49,
          "en": "because I want to filter on the status property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 338.49,
          "end": 340.65,
          "en": "Now if we save this and reload the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 340.65,
          "end": 343.56,
          "en": "you see no servers are displayed by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 343.56,
          "end": 346.40999999999997,
          "en": "because no servers match this criteria.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 346.40999999999997,
          "end": 348.27,
          "en": "If I type stable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 348.27,
          "end": 350.49,
          "en": "you see we see the stable server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 350.49,
          "end": 351.81,
          "en": "but that doesn't look correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 351.81,
          "end": 355.35,
          "en": "because we should have more than one stable server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 355.35,
          "end": 357.27,
          "en": "If we have a look at our app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 357.27,
          "end": 359.34000000000003,
          "en": "we get free stable servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 359.34000000000003,
          "end": 361.74,
          "en": "So we only view the first one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 361.74,
          "end": 365.79,
          "en": "and the reason for this is simply that right now here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 365.79,
          "end": 367.77,
          "en": "I'm returning inside of this for loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 367.77,
          "end": 370.35,
          "en": "so this is a little logical mistake here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 370.35,
          "end": 372.6,
          "en": "We should of course return outside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 372.6,
          "end": 376.29,
          "en": "and also create this array outside of it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 376.29,
          "end": 378.51,
          "en": "So with this change in place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 378.51,
          "end": 380.91,
          "en": "now we should see that once we add stable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 380.91,
          "end": 382.62,
          "en": "we see all stable servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 382.62,
          "end": 385.86,
          "en": "And once we add offline, we see the offline server.",
          "zh": ""
